# The same shields, in a SMALL character's hand. Bead inc-rsps.
#
# WHY A SECOND FILE. tools/keys/shield-penalty.keys reads the figure
# lib/weapons.irh authors, which is what a MEDIUM character pays. The size
# step in Armour::PenaltyVal (src/Item.cpp) is the other half of the rule: a
# smaller bearer carries relatively more shield, so his figure doubles. Three
# playable races are Small -- halfling, gnome and kobold -- so this is a case
# a player reaches, not a corner.
#
# THE SUBJECT is a halfling warrior, made here rather than by including one of
# the chargen scripts because none of them makes a Small character. He gets
# TWO skill pools, one for the class and one after the god, which is why the
# skill loop appears twice; a warrior's feats are a loop for the same reason.
#
# ONLY THE BUCKLER AND THE SMALL SHIELD ARE READ. A Small character cannot get
# a kite shield into his hand at all -- the attempt leaves the previous shield
# where it was -- and the tower shield is further out of reach still. Say so
# rather than let a silent skip look like a reading.
#
# THE ORACLE is the Movement Rate line's shield factor, not the Skill Ratings
# armour term. The halfling wears studded leather, which carries a penalty of
# its own and is summed into the armour term; the movement line prints the
# shield's share on its own, so it needs no subtraction to be believed.
#
# Menu letters move when a list changes. Run at the seed the check supplies.

a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Your options will place the game in Explore Mode. Continue? -- yes

@choose "Halfling"
a       # Subrace: [a] Halfling (Standard)
@choose "Warrior"
a       # Attributes: the first of the offered sets
a       # Alignment:  the first offered

@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "|  *" RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT DOWN
ENTER y
@while "wish to worship" y
@while "|  *" RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT DOWN
ENTER y
@while "personality archetype" a
@until "Afoot" ESC

w
@expect "Enter wizard mode"
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN
SPACE           # Auto-Identify Items
ESC

# Shields are the seventeenth entry of ItemGlyphs (src/Tables.cpp:320-337).
# The list is Tower, Kite, Small, Buckler, Buckler and opens on the first row.

# --- BUCKLER ----------------------------------------------------------------
w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*16
DOWN DOWN DOWN
ENTER
a
SPACE
@dump:buckler-in-hand
ESC
d
W
b u c k
ENTER
ESC

# --- SMALL SHIELD -----------------------------------------------------------
w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*16
DOWN DOWN
ENTER
a
SPACE
@dump:small-in-hand
ESC
d
W
s m a l l
ENTER
ESC
@quit
